## Goal
Create a complete recipe markdown file in `content/Recepten` using the template at `content/templates/recipe_template_v1.md`. Populate all template variables from details given in the chat, or extract them from a link provided in the conversation.

## Trigger
- When the user asks to add/write/create a recipe.
- Or when the user provides a recipe (directly in chat or via a link) and asks to save it.

## Output location and filename
- Save to: `content/Recepten/<Title>.md`
- Use the recipe title for `<Title>` as written by the user (retain spaces and punctuation used elsewhere in this repository).

## Template to use
- Base file: `content/templates/recipe_template_v1.md`
- Do not change headings in the template (Dutch labels must remain as-is).

## Data mapping (required fields)
Collect and map these fields using Obsidian-style YAML frontmatter for properties, and keep only ingredients/instructions in the body.

- Frontmatter (Obsidian properties)
  - `tags`: YAML list (one per line). If unspecified, leave empty or omit.
  - `created`: ISO date string `YYYY-MM-DD`. If missing, use today's date (project timezone).
  - `author`: string. If missing, prefer repository owner or the user who provided the recipe; otherwise leave blank.
  - `url`: source URL if the recipe was provided via a link; otherwise leave blank.
  - `cookTime`: total active + passive time if available; otherwise active cook time. Prefer a human string like `ca. 45 min`.
  - `recipeYield`: servings/portion text (e.g., `4 personen`).
  - `image`: filename under `content/Recepten/Afbeeldingen` or a URL.
  - `description`: 1–3 sentences summarizing the dish.

- Body content
  - `recipeIngredient`: array of strings, one per ingredient line. Preserve given quantities and units. Group with optional `####` subkoppen (bijv. `Vulling`, `Deeg`).
  - `recipeInstructions`: steps. If the recipe has sections, structure as an array of sections with `name` and `itemListElement` of step texts. Otherwise, provide a flat array of step texts.

## Parsing from link (if URL is provided)
1. Fetch the page and extract title, description, image, servings, time, ingredients, and instructions.
2. Normalize lists: remove numbering from ingredients; keep numbering for instructions in the final render via the template.
3. Preserve original order and section grouping when present.

## File creation steps
1. Confirm or infer: title, tags, created, author, url, cookTime, recipeYield, image, description, ingredients, instructions.
2. Create `content/Recepten/<Title>.md` using `content/templates/recipe_template_v1.md` as a starting point.
3. Convert to Obsidian properties:
   - Move `cookTime`, `recipeYield`, `image`, and `description` into the YAML frontmatter (above `---`).
   - Represent `tags` as a YAML list (one per line).
   - Remove the body lines that duplicate these properties (the lines beginning with `Bereidingstijd:`, `Recept voor:`, the image embed, and the description paragraph directly under them).
4. Keep body sections and headings in Dutch. Populate ingredients and instructions:
   - Under `### Ingredienten`, optionally split into `####` subkoppen (bijv. `Vulling`, `Deeg`).
   - Under `### Instructies`, keep numbered steps; use `####` subkoppen for sections when needed.
5. For images placed in the vault, prefer relative Obsidian embeds like `![[<bestandsnaam>|500]]`. Ensure the filename matches the file saved under `content/Recepten/Afbeeldingen/`.

## Quality and formatting rules
- Write all recipe content in Dutch. If the source is not Dutch, translate faithfully.
- Keep existing template headings in Dutch: `### Ingredienten`, `### Instructies`, `## Aantekeningen`.
- Preserve user-provided punctuation, units, and capitalization.
- Do not add explanatory comments into the recipe file beyond the template’s structure.
- Use UTF-8 and keep line endings consistent with the repo.
- When assigning tags, prefer values from `.cursor/data/recipe_tags.yaml` (merge multiple relevant groups: course, cuisine, main_ingredient, method, diet, occasion, misc). Keep tags lowercase.

## Example fill (structure only; not a literal snippet)
- Frontmatter keys: `tags`, `created`, `author`, `url`.
- Body fields mapped as above; sections appear as `#### <Section Name>` rendered by the template.

## If data is incomplete
- Ask concise follow-up questions in chat for the missing critical fields: title, ingredients, and instructions.
- For optional fields (image, tags, url, description, cookTime, recipeYield), proceed without them if not available.

